{"completed": true, "response": "<escape>{\n  \"report_supported\": \"partly\",\n  \"judge_supported\": \"yes\",\n  \"report_quotes\": [\n    \"The finding of impaired, short-term efficacy in tremor suppression by non-continuous DBS was interpreted as the inability to mask burst-driver inputs to the thalamus.\",\n    \"This might partially explain the slightly inferior short-term effect on objective gait parameters and the FoG-Course of TBS-DBS as a whole group compared to cDBS.\",\n    \"TBS-DBS with its temporal patterning might slowly, progressively increase its subthalamic efficacy in the long-term by beneficial neuroplastic effects from TBS-DBS.\",\n    \"Since axial symptoms might change over days, the EEG might potentially point to advantageous long-term changes, which could not be proven in that acute experimental setting.\",\n    \"However, these effects only become apparent after a longer period of stimulation. For the exploration of the full effect strength, a long-term evaluation of TBS-DBS would be necessary, which has not been performed here in the randomised study of short-term effects.\"\n  ],\n  \"judge_quotes\": [\n    \"In this monocentric, randomised, double-blind, short-term study, 12 age-matched controls (11 male, age 59 ± 8 years) and 15 PD participants (14 male, age 62 ± 9 years, disease duration 15 ± 6 years) with subthalamic stimulation (76 ± 39 months) were assessed with clinical scores (FoG-Course, MDS-UPDRS) and a standardized gait course simulating everyday life situations.\",\n    \"Three DBS algorithms were applied in a randomized order with intertrial waiting periods of 30 min: (1) OFF-DBS; (2) cDBS; (3) TBS-DBS (interburst frequency 5 Hz, intraburst frequency 200 Hz) with regular medication.\",\n    \"The primary outcome, the relative change of FoG-Course by DBS, was not superior with TBS-DBS compared to cDBS in the entire sample.\",\n    \"During the standardized gait course a mobile, 24-channel EEG system and 6 wearable axial kinematic sensors were used.\",\n    \"EEG data were segmented into 1 s non-overlapping epochs to compare episodes of straight walking, FoG and resting-like condition (30s EEG recording while the patient is sitting on a chair with eyes open before starting the FoG-Course) among participants.\",\n    \"In an exploratory analysis, we also calculated a cluster permutation test between regular walking and freezing episodes where no significant clusters were found.\",\n    \"The most important limitation in the evaluation of patterned DBS algorithms is the assessment of short-term effects of TBS-DBS on gait within one day, since the effects of patterned DBS might evolve over time and axial symptoms typically respond over a longer time course.\",\n    \"For the exploration of the full effect strength, a long-term evaluation of TBS-DBS would be necessary, which has not been performed here in the randomised study of short-term effects.\"\n  ],\n  \"why\": \"报告的两项说法均能在论文Discussion中找到文字依据，因此不能判定为与全文不符。但这些依据有决定性限定条件。H19方面，论文引用的是非连续丘脑DBS期间震颤重新出现及无法遮蔽丘脑burst-driver输入的既往研究，并将其作为解释TBS-DBS短期步态效果可能较差的一种推测。论文没有直接验证STN-FOG事件中的暂停期刺激遮蔽机制。H20方面，论文确实提出TBS-DBS可能通过神经可塑性逐渐增强长期丘脑底核疗效，也提出轴性症状可能随时间、跨日发生变化，但明确说明这些长期效应尚未在本研究中得到验证，且需要长期研究。因此，若报告将这两项机制表述为该研究提出的理论假设或可能解释，有全文依据；若将其作为该研究已经实验证实的机制，则缺少改变结论的关键限定，属于证据强度和研究结论范围的扩大。指控者的描述总体准确。需要补充一个细节：论文确实利用头皮EEG比较了行走与FoG阶段的皮层活动，但没有直接记录STN-LFP，也没有专门测量STN-FOG事件中刺激暂停期的神经活动。论文还明确指出，长期评价并未进行。因此，最终判断为report_supported=partly，judge_supported=yes。\"\n}</escape>", "metadata": {"session_handle": "34e6f9b0-6ede-4151-9230-5db4454abd70", "session_revision": 0, "session_ttl_max_hours": 6, "job_directory": "D:\\musicclaude\\gpt2agent-safechain\\runs\\gpt3\\pro-bridge-20261114T071124256261Z", "elapsed_seconds": 97.391, "completed_utc": "2026-11-14T07:13:01.666411+00:00", "model": "gpt-6-thinking", "thinking_effort": "max", "temporary": true, "unpersonalized": true, "generation_policy_verified": true, "request_policy": {"model": "gpt-6-thinking", "thinking_effort": "max", "history_and_training_disabled": true, "temporary_chat_requests_personalization": false, "is_do_not_remember": false, "continuation": false, "unpersonalized_inherited_verified": false, "body_sha256": "f10f0e82d5dccd855fe8c8b0919b08ec04c35c35d898ed18248fccdb92f087a2", "attachment_count": 1}, "stream_completion": {"sse_done": true, "message_completed": true, "independent_terminal_verified": true}, "profile": "yi/local-codex-auth", "account_sha256": "b3efb6361563c139233ed7b7ef61a7c9afe0bd48d4eb3525dbe31956b024d6da", "transport": "probridge-pure-http", "resume_requests": 0, "topic_connections": 0, "browser_started": false, "Docker_used": false, "automatic_retry": false, "initializer_pss_limit_mib": "not_applicable_no_browser", "attachment_count": 1, "code_sha256": {"tools\\chatgpt_web\\gpt3_cli.py": "96a4cdb6cd5d982f4d1de5b6ba8fae0cf23ee44aa3e41d7fdf6968e3fb590e48", "tools\\chatgpt_web\\gpt3_sessions.py": "83a3ed4ae1efa9f1a2b8ee3f144cc0dc9f668f995a33cc4222308cb3fa31f683", "tools\\chatgpt_web\\gpt3_attachments.py": "eedfa23885000025700f6306b1d1f4582896a7370734be506c156dee532fd7d7"}}, "screenshot_evidence": {"complete": true, "kind": "offline_actual_HTTP_response", "directory": "D:\\musicclaude\\gpt2agent-safechain\\runs\\gpt3\\pro-bridge-20261114T071124256261Z", "files": ["proof-offline.png"], "sha256": {"proof-offline.png": "1b4ef80680604712b5f173b54a3193d8748423bc718794004577ca215fabf752"}}}
